issues.body:
`Service.List` doesn't define an order. InMemory returns ID order, and Database runs `Find` with no ORDER BY, so on Postgres the order can shift after updates. adk-python pinned this to last update time, oldest first (google/adk-python#6276, 53e1afbc), after a Postgres user lost history picking `sessions[-1]` (google/adk-python#6272). No Go reports that I know of, and the downstream projects I checked sort themselves.

Failing tests for in-memory and database (SQLite) on current main are below:
- in-memory: `List() session order = [a b c], want [b c a]`
- database: `List() order = [a b c], want [b a c]`

Happy to PR: document the order, sort in memory, ORDER BY in database. Should the exported conformance suite assert it too? That would fail third-party implementations.

<details><summary>session/inmemory_test.go</summary>

```go
func TestInMemoryService_ListOrderedByLastUpdateTime(t *testing.T) {
	s := session.InMemoryService()
	base := time.Date(2026, 1, 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, time.UTC)
	at := func(d time.Duration) context.Context {
		return platform.WithTimeProvider(t.Context(), func() time.Time { return base.Add(d) })
	}
	created := map[string]session.Session{}
	for i, id := range []string{"a", "b", "c"} {
		resp, err := s.Create(at(time.Duration(i)*time.Second), &session.CreateRequest{AppName: "app", UserID: "u", SessionID: id})
		if err != nil {
			t.Fatal(err)
		}
		created[id] = resp.Session
	}
	// Make the oldest session the most recently active one.
	ev := session.NewEvent(t.Context(), "inv")
	ev.Timestamp = base.Add(time.Minute)
	if err := s.AppendEvent(t.Context(), created["a"], ev); err != nil {
		t.Fatal(err)
	}

	resp, err := s.List(t.Context(), &session.ListRequest{AppName: "app", UserID: "u"})
	if err != nil {
		t.Fatal(err)
	}
	var got []string
	for _, sess := range resp.Sessions {
		got = append(got, sess.ID())
	}
	if want := []string{"b", "c", "a"}; !slices.Equal(got, want) {
		t.Errorf("List() session order = %v, want %v (oldest update first)", got, want)
	}
}
```
</details>

