issues.body:
## 🔴 Required Information

**Describe the Bug:**

In `RunLive`, the function response for a tool call is written straight to the connection from the main loop ([base_flow.go#L703-L708](https://github.com/google/adk-go/blob/40d37cad8feffd20f6790961a604789b9b5049ac/internal/llminternal/base_flow.go#L703-L708)). It does not go through the sender goroutine and `errChan`, so `isResumable` never sees an error from that write, and nothing sends the response again after a reconnect. If the connection drops while a tool is running, one of two things happens:

1. The write fails and the session ends with that error, even for a drop that is resumed when no tool is in flight. After a TCP reset, the error that ends the session is one `isResumable` itself reports as resumable.
2. The write does not fail (after a hard close it lands in the socket buffer). The flow reconnects as it should, but the function response is never sent on the new connection, so the model's call is left without an answer.

@karolpiotrowicz pointed at this send in his review of #1603.

**Steps to Reproduce:**

1. Use the fake Live server from `base_flow_live_test.go`. Connection 1 sends one `toolCall`, waits 50ms, then drops in one of the ways below. Connection 2 records whether it receives the tool response, then sends a model turn.
2. The tool sleeps either 0s or 300ms. With 0s the response goes out before the drop, which is the control.
3. Run the test below from `internal/llminternal`.

**Expected Behavior:**

A drop while a tool runs is handled like the same drop with no tool running. If it is resumable, the flow reconnects and the function response is delivered on the new connection.

**Observed Behavior:**

Same results on Windows and Linux:

| Drop on connection 1 | tool returned before the drop | tool still running at the drop |
| --- | --- | --- |
| hard close | reconnects | reconnects, connection 2 never gets the tool response |
| TCP reset (`SetLinger(0)`) | reconnects | session ends: `failed to send tool response: write tcp ...: write: broken pipe` on Linux, `wsasend: An existing connection was forcibly closed by the remote host.` on Windows. `isResumable` returns true for this error |
| close frame 1008 | reconnects | session ends: `failed to send tool response: websocket: close sent` |
| close frame 1001 or 1011 | session ends (reader: `close 1001` / `close 1011`) | session ends: `failed to send tool response: websocket: close sent` |

The 1001 and 1011 rows end the session either way, so they don't show the problem. They're there to show which side reports the error.

**Environment Details:**

 - ADK Library Version: main at 40d37ca
 - OS: Windows 10 and Linux (WSL2, Ubuntu 24.04)
 - Go Version: 1.26.6

**Model Information:**
 - Which model is being used: N/A (fake Live server)

---

## 🟡 Optional Information

**Regression:**

Not as far as I can tell. The send is the same back to the oldest commit in my clone (6789f7a, 2026-07-28).

**Additional Context:**

adk-python puts the function response on `live_request_queue` ([_live_llm_flow.py](https://github.com/google/adk-python/blob/main/src/google/adk/live/_live_llm_flow.py)). That queue outlives the connection, each connection's send task drains it, and a `ConnectionClosed` in the receive loop goes to the reconnect path. That is from reading the code. I did not run it, and I don't know whether it re-sends a response that was already written to a dead socket either.

I see two ways to fix it, and I'd like a maintainer's view before opening a PR since this is in the live flow:

- Send the function response through the sender goroutine, or report its error on `errChan`, so one classification decides.
- Keep the last function response the server has not answered and send it again after a reconnect. This one needs a call on duplicates: after a hard close the flow can't tell whether the server got the first write.

Not checked: what the Live API does with a resumed session whose last function call never got a response.

I haven't probed the history send at [L540-L552](https://github.com/google/adk-go/blob/40d37cad8feffd20f6790961a604789b9b5049ac/internal/llminternal/base_flow.go#L540-L552), but from reading it, it runs on every connection, including redials, and a failed write there also ends the session without going through `isResumable`.

**Minimal Reproduction Code:**

<details>
<summary>Probe test (drop into <code>internal/llminternal</code>, uses the helpers from <code>base_flow_live_test.go</code> and <code>live_reconnect_test.go</code>)</summary>

```go
package llminternal

import (
	"fmt"
	"iter"
	"net"
	"strings"
	"sync"
	"sync/atomic"
	"testing"
	"time"

	"github.com/gorilla/websocket"

	"google.golang.org/adk/v2/agent"
	"google.golang.org/adk/v2/model"
	"google.golang.org/adk/v2/session"
	"google.golang.org/adk/v2/tool"
)

func TestLiveDropWhileToolRuns(t *testing.T) {
	const toolCall = `{"toolCall":{"functionCalls":[{"id":"c1","name":"slow_job","args":{}}]}}`
	cases := []struct {
		name string
		drop func(conn *websocket.Conn)
	}{
		{"hard close", func(conn *websocket.Conn) {}},
		{"close frame 1001 then hard close", func(conn *websocket.Conn) {
			_ = conn.WriteMessage(websocket.CloseMessage, websocket.FormatCloseMessage(websocket.CloseGoingAway, "going away"))
		}},
		{"close frame 1011 then hard close", func(conn *websocket.Conn) {
			_ = conn.WriteMessage(websocket.CloseMessage, websocket.FormatCloseMessage(websocket.CloseInternalServerErr, "internal"))
		}},
		{"close frame 1008 then hard close", func(conn *websocket.Conn) {
			_ = conn.WriteMessage(websocket.CloseMessage, websocket.FormatCloseMessage(websocket.ClosePolicyViolation, "policy"))
		}},
		{"RST", func(conn *websocket.Conn) {
			if tcp, ok := conn.NetConn().(*net.TCPConn); ok {
				_ = tcp.SetLinger(0)
			}
		}},
	}
	for _, tc := range cases {
		for _, toolDelay := range []time.Duration{0, 300 * time.Millisecond} {
			t.Run(fmt.Sprintf("%s/tool %v", tc.name, toolDelay), func(t *testing.T) {
				var gotToolResponseOn sync.Map
				client, connCount := startFakeLiveServer(t, func(connNum int, conn *websocket.Conn) {
					if connNum == 1 {
						if err := conn.WriteMessage(websocket.TextMessage, []byte(toolCall)); err != nil {
							return
						}
						time.Sleep(50 * time.Millisecond) // the tool is running now
						tc.drop(conn)
						return
					}
					_ = conn.SetReadDeadline(time.Now().Add(time.Second))
					for {
						_, msg, err := conn.ReadMessage()
						if err != nil {
							break
						}
						if strings.Contains(string(msg), "slow_job") {
							gotToolResponseOn.Store(connNum, true)
						}
					}
					_ = conn.WriteMessage(websocket.TextMessage, []byte(serverContentPong))
					blockUntilClientCloses(conn)
				})
				var ran atomic.Int32
				f := &Flow{
					Model:             &fakeLiveModel{client: client},
					RequestProcessors: []func(ctx agent.InvocationContext, req *model.LLMRequest, f *Flow) iter.Seq2[*session.Event, error]{liveConfigProcessor},
					Tools: []tool.Tool{
						&mockFunctionTool{name: "slow_job", runFunc: func(agent.Context, map[string]any) (map[string]any, error) {
							ran.Add(1)
							time.Sleep(toolDelay)
							return map[string]any{"ok": true}, nil
						}},
					},
					reconnect: testLiveReconnectPolicy(4, 20),
				}
				ctx, cancel := newLiveInvocationContext(t)
				defer cancel()
				sess, seq, err := f.RunLive(ctx)
				if err != nil {
					t.Fatalf("RunLive: %v", err)
				}
				var streamErr error
				sawPong := make(chan struct{})
				var wg sync.WaitGroup
				wg.Add(1)
				go func() {
					defer wg.Done()
					once := false
					for ev, err := range seq {
						if err != nil && streamErr == nil {
							streamErr = err
						}
						if ev != nil && ev.LLMResponse.Content != nil && !once {
							for _, p := range ev.LLMResponse.Content.Parts {
								if p.Text == "pong" {
									once = true
									close(sawPong)
								}
							}
						}
					}
				}()
				served := false
				select {
				case <-sawPong:
					served = true
				case <-time.After(5 * time.Second):
				}
				_ = sess.Close()
				wg.Wait()
				_, resent := gotToolResponseOn.Load(2)
				errType := ""
				if streamErr != nil {
					errType = fmt.Sprintf("%T", streamErr)
				}
				t.Logf("RESULT tool ran=%d dials=%d served-after-drop=%v toolResponse-on-conn2=%v streamErr=%v (%s) isResumable(streamErr)=%v",
					ran.Load(), connCount.Load(), served, resent, streamErr, errType, isResumable(streamErr))
			})
		}
	}
}
```

</details>

**How often has this issue occurred?:**

 - Always (100%) with the probe above

